<!-- SCE Forge conformance: Zenoh linkstate-peer routing — a single
     `links` element (a neighbour peer-state-id reference, VLE u64).

     Mirrors the per-element write/read inside zenoh
     `zenoh/src/net/codec/linkstate.rs:70-73` / `:114-119`:

         codec.write(&mut *writer, x.links.len())?;   // count (VLE)
         for l in x.links.iter() {
             codec.write(&mut *writer, *l)?;           // each link = VLE u64
         }

     The `links` field is `Vec<u64>` — a bare list of base-128 VLE u64
     psid references with NO per-element wrapper struct on the wire.
     SCE's `<sce:repeat type=...>` accepts only an imported CODEC alias
     as its element type (sce-build parser.rs: the repeat body `type`
     resolves against the import table, never a primitive `sce:type`),
     so a bare-scalar repeat is not expressible. This 1-field codec is
     the minimal wrapper that makes the element a codec — byte-identical
     to a bare VLE u64, exactly as `locator.scxml` wraps a bare
     length-prefixed string for the locator-list repeat in `hello`.

     Wire shape:
       byte 0+ : psid  (VLE u64, 1..=10 bytes — a neighbour link-state's
                        psid, the small-int node id used by the spanning
                        -tree / shortest-path graph in net/protocol/
                        network.rs).

     Composition: B1-alpha VLE only (same single-field shape as
     ext_zint). No new primitive surface. -->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:sce="http://sce.dev/ext"
       sce:kind="codec" sce:default-endian="big" name="linkstate_link">
  <datamodel>
    <sce:field id="psid" sce:type="uint64" sce:byte="0" sce:bit-size="vle"/>
  </datamodel>
</scxml>
